<h1>ABSTRACT</h1>
<p>The challenge of gadget affordability remains a significant barrier to digital literacy and economic participation among Nigerian students. This research presents "Zenda," a specialized fintech platform designed to automate the process of gadget acquisition through installments. The system addresses the core issues of credit risk and payment default by integrating automated Know Your Customer (KYC) verification, real time logistics tracking, and a secure escrow settlement mechanism. The application architecture utilizes a React.js frontend, a Node.js backend, and a PostgreSQL database managed via Supabase. The study demonstrates how automated credit scoring based on user profile data can reduce the reliance on traditional collateral, thereby increasing financial inclusion for the youth population. Results show that the system successfully manages the entire purchase lifecycle, from vendor product listing to final customer settlement, with high accuracy and security.</p>

